Practice files for the LPI Essentials questions
-----------------------------------------------

test.sh          A script without the execute bit. Run ./test.sh,
                 fix it with chmod, and run it again. Also try
                 bash test.sh.
script.sh        Prints $MYVAR. Compare "MYVAR=value; ./script.sh"
                 with "export MYVAR=value; ./script.sh".
Downloads/       An empty directory. Try rm, rmdir and rm -r on it.
Documents/       From ~/Downloads, which directory does
                 ls ../Documents/ show?
texts/           "texts 1.txt", "texts 2.txt" and "texts 3.csv".
                 Which glob copies only the .txt files to /tmp/?
loop/            a.txt, b.txt and c.cav, for:
                 for file in *.txt; do echo $file; done
Texts 2.txt      A name with a space. How many ways can you cat it?
data.csv         Unsorted lines for sort, wc, head, tail and cut.
operating-systems.txt
                 For grep, grep -i and grep -c.
work/            A directory to archive with tar, gzip and bzip2,
                 and to list with ls -R.
doku.odt         Make tux its owner. Create the user first, as root:
                 su -, then useradd -m tux.

Also worth a look: ls -l /tmp, ls /proc, cat /etc/passwd, id,
ls -l /etc/skel, free -h, top, dmesg | head, last, echo $PATH,
find /home -name '*.txt'.
